 ## How it works
-The method operates in two primary modes depending on the underlying architecture: the ICON approach for NeRF-based radiance fields [S2] and the ZeroGS approach for 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, unofficial]. Both follow the shared principles of metric computation, expansion triggers, and re-optimization defined in [Parent](8869-progressive-and-dynamic-scene-growth.md).
+The method adapts to the underlying scene representation architecture, primarily implemented for NeRF-based radiance fields [S2] and 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, unofficial]. Both variants follow the shared principles of metric computation, expansion triggers, and re-optimization defined in [Progressive and Dynamic Scene Growth](8869-progressive-and-dynamic-scene-growth.md).
 
